ill take.\n\nAs teacher educators, we teach many of Calkins' (2010) writing strategies, including her approach to teacher-student writing conferences, in our literacy methods courses. In our own previous experiences as public school teachers, we practiced teaching writing through a workshop approach according to progressive literacy research (Graves, 1983;Murray, 1985;Myers & Whitmore, in press). We and the classroom teachers agreed that an intervention strategy for improving student writing would be to focus on the student-teacher writing conference, providing more",
