      "snippet": {
        "text": "This study also examined the moderating effect of teacher support on the process of 'episodic future thinkingintrinsic motivation-engagement in learning' , and the results indicated that teacher support moderated the relationship between intrinsic motivation and learning engagement. This finding is generally consistent with existing research that teacher support, as a key external factor, facilitates students' academic adjustment and is positively related to students' motivation to participate in class, their interest in learning, and their foreign language achievement 79,80 . Compared with students with lower levels of teacher support, intrinsic motivation and engagement can be more facilitated when students' intrinsic needs for relatedness, competence, and autonomy are supported by teachers in the classroom 81 . Students' perceptions of teacher support in the external environment can be transformed into psychological capital in the process of intrinsic motivation, which creates a synergistic force to promote their learning engagement and thus helps succeed academically 82 . This suggests that the key role of teacher support as a guide to learning helps to stimulate students' motivation to engage in learning, and then form a mutually supportive and interactive operating mechanism. Therefore, colleges and universities should not only pay attention to providing students with a good hardware environment, but also link up all the forces to build a scientific and reasonable teacher support system that promotes students' engagement in learning. \n\nSpecifically, as an important external driver for students to translate motivation into behavior, good teacher affection support is demonstrated to be teacher's continuous transmission of a sense of conviction conducive to the formation of students' positive emotional loading 83 , therefore, sensitively capturing students' personalities and giving them positive feedback can narrow the distance between teacher and students, and enhance the emotional link. In terms of capacity support, \"it is critical for teachers to create learning environment that boosts students' learning motivation and allows learners to self-regulate their learning\" (p. 10) 84 , therefore teachers need to scaffold students' learning experience by recommending, using, or incorporating learning resources in classroom activities that are more likely to be adopted by students 56 . From the perspective of behavior support, language learning is a process that follows from object regulation to others' regulation to self-regulation 85 .",
