      "snippet": {
        "text": "Another significant AI application in education is conversational AI, which includes chatbots and dialogue-based AI tutors designed to facilitate student engagement and scaffold learning. Recent studies have explored how AI-powered dialogue systems can support collaborative writing, legal writing instruction, and discussion-based learning. For example, CollaBot, a conversational AI agent developed by Hu, Tian, and Li (2025), was designed to support collaborative writing activities in online courses. The study found that while CollaBot did not significantly improve students' behavioral or emotional engagement, it enhanced cognitive engagement by encouraging students to explain concepts more thoroughly and structure their writing more effectively. \n\nSimilarly, AI-driven legal writing assistants have been developed to support law students in academic writing. Weber, Wambsganss, and Söllner (2024) introduced LegalWriter, a fine-tuned BERT-based AI model designed to provide real-time feedback on legal essays. \n\nThe study found that students using the AI tool demonstrated significant improvements in argument structure and persuasive writing. Additionally, Chen et al. (2025) conducted a comparative study evaluating the effectiveness of AI vs. human experts in supporting reading-to-writing tasks. Their findings revealed that while AI feedback was efficient and accessible, human experts provided deeper conceptual insights, reinforcing the importance of hybrid AI-human tutoring models.",
