      "snippet": {
        "text": "In conclusion, keeping all these in mind it is \"necessary to improve the way lecturers teach in class because teaching method is another factor that causes students not to succeed in mastering essay writing skills\" (Salikin et al., 2017, p. 85). \n\nAccording to Fernandez et al. (2017), three types of issues can arise when students learn to write for academic purposes: attitudinal, cognitive, and social issues, all of which affect the quality of their writing. Tarrayo et al. (2021) state the urgent need for innovation in language teaching, including those related to 21st-century skills, digital literacy, and technology integration, which means that online or flexible learning and teaching have become necessary. What is more, Barret et al. (2019) claim that the field of education is becoming aware of the necessity to successfully integrate AI for both staff and students because better student experiences can be achieved by utilizing artificial intelligence. Cotton et al. (2024) state that AI systems and chatbots are promising advancement in technology that has the potential to increase work pace and efficiency in daily routine. Alharbi (2023) confirms that AI-powered writing assistance tools can help students improve their writing skills because they can provide students with individualized learning possibilities by detecting their writing capabilities and deficiencies (Bhutoria, 2022). \n\nWhen considering the theoretical frameworks underpinning this study, the relevance between AI tools and the improvement of the writing skill of foreign language becomes prevalent. Accordingly, this study was conducted in the School of Foreign Languages of a state university in Istanbul, focusing on Turkish learners of English seeking to improve their academic English skills including \"writing\". In the context of integrating technology into language learning, writing, as a fundamental component of academic success and professional communication, has increasingly become a focal point of research. As highlighted in the subsequent sections, most of the studies conducted concentrated on how AI tools improved the writing skill of language learners. Thus, the present study shifts the focus on to the perceptions of English language instructors who teach learners using AI tools to improve their writing skills both for academic purposes and future professional lives. This focus is particularly significant in the Turkish context, where limited empirical research exists on the integration of AI tools into English language teaching.",
