      "snippet": {
        "text": "Artificial intelligence (AI) emerged as a disruptive technology in multiple disciplines since the release of ChatGPT in 2022. 1 ChatGPT is a sophisticated AI language model developed by OpenAI. It can understand and generate human-like text, making it capable of engaging in natural and coherent conversations on a wide range of topics (note these prior two sentences were written by ChatGPT). The large language model (LLM) technology used by ChatGPT offers the potential to streamline routine tasks including writing essays for college admissions and term articles for humanities classes. 2 However, AI has also been proposed for teaching in the STEM fields. \n\nSimilar to ChatGPT, other types of Intelligent systems have been incorporated into STEM classrooms in higher education to facilitate student learning. A systematic review of the use of AI in higher education showed that AI has been implemented in classrooms to teach, grade, provide feedback to students, in addition to supporting teachers in lecture and classroom designs. 3  specific study conducted in 2013 used an AI Inquire Biology textbook system that answers student questions and showed that AI use in the classroom engaged students and improved learning outcomes. 4 Another study showed the use of an intelligent tutoring system in medicine, specifically dermatopathology. This study taught histopathologic diagnosis and reporting skills based on commonly used diagnostic algorithms. The results indicated that the students benefited from the system and the frequency of student errors were reduced. 5 The use of AI to generate multiple choice questions has also been explored previously. A study in 2006 created a program that could successfully generate questions for Basque language exams. 6 The results showed that this specifically designed system was able to generate proper questions 80 % of the time. Another study in 2022 was able to design a program that could take raw text as input and produce multiple choice questions from the raw text. 7 This was accomplished by first having the program process the text, summarize it, score topics, and then generate multiple choice questions using the selected text. T e actual generation of the question involved the creation of a question stem followed by generation of correct answers and incorrect answers, called distractors in the study. Similar to the previously mentioned study, the authors focused on a single topic (in this case computer science), but subsequently were able to generate questions from any raw unedited text.",
