      "snippet": {
        "text": "This study was conducted using Generative Pre-trained Transformer 4 (GPT-4). GPT-4 is a multimodal large language model developed by OpenAI. The first GPT was introduced in 2018 and various iterations of GPT existed prior to the release of GPT-4 on 3/13/2023. GPT-4 has been trained on a vast dataset, enabling it to process and generate text with unprecedented contextual information. GPT-4 has a wide range of applications, from automating customer service interactions to aiding in complex data analysis tasks (Marr, 2023). \n\nIn this study we utilized GPT-4 to generate text. GPT-4 is a subscription plan offered by OpenAI for users of ChatGPT service. It is designed to provide subscribers with several benefits over the free version of ChatGPT including the use of the latest generative mode. \n\nWe began by asking GPT-4 to write an APA paper on a topic relevant to school psychology and AI. Our prompt was based on the prompt used by Marchandot (2023). We provided a 2500-word limit, as this is typically the limit for brief articles in our field. To do so, we entered the following prompt on 3/22/2023: Write a 2500-word manuscript on the ethical dilemmas of using ChatGPT to write for psychological and educational reports. Address how APA and NASP guidelines, as well as HIPAA and FERPA laws pertain to these ethical dilemmas. Provide recommendations for overcoming these limitations. Provide citations and references in APA formatting. \n\nBecause several claims made by GPT-4 were not sufficiently explained, we provided five incremental prompts consisting of \"explain how [text]… Provide citations and references in APA formatting,\" were then provided for assertions made by GPT-4 that needed expanding. For example, we prompted \"'explain how a ChatGPT AI model may inadvertently store, transmit, or expose sensitive client information during the report-writing process' in one to three sentences.",
