      "snippet": {
        "text": "These findings suggest that ChatGPT can serve as a valuable tool not only for enhancing how learners approach and view writing but also for supporting tangible improvements in critical aspects of written composition. Similarly, Athanassopoulos et al. (2023) and Song and Song (2023) observed gains in vocabulary, grammar, and overall language proficiency among L2 and EFL learners. In addition to supporting learners, ChatGPT can assist educators in areas such as guiding the writing process (Barret & Pack, 2023), and writing assessment (Mizumoto et al., 2024). Teng (2024b) explored the perspectives and experiences of 45 EFL learners in Macao regarding the use of ChatGPT for writing feedback through questionnaires. To gain deeper insights, semi-structured interviews were conducted with eight students who actively used the AI tool. The findings indicated that ChatGPT had a notably positive impact, boosting learners' motivation, enhancing their sense of self-efficacy, increasing engagement, and fostering collaborative behaviors. This study highlights the potential of AI-driven tools to transform the writing process by not only improving technical skills but also promoting a more dynamic and interactive learning experience. In a separate study, Teng (2024c) investigated 40 EFL undergraduates over the course of a semester-long writing program. Data were collected through questionnaires and interviews. Quantitative analysis showed significant improvements in learners' writing experiences and perceptions, particularly in areas such as writing motivation, engagement, self-efficacy, and collaborative writing tendencies. Moreover, a positive correlation was identified between learners' metacognitive awareness (MA) scores and their perceptions and use of ChatGPT. Qualitative findings further suggested that students with higher metacognitive awareness demonstrated greater motivation and engagement when interacting with ChatGPT. Zou et al. (2024) investigated how ChatGPT supports EFL learners in improving their language skills. The study utilized an extended version of the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM) to examine the internal and external factors shaping learners' willingness to embrace ChatGPT for enhancing their oral English abilities. Data were collected through surveys from 212 Chinese EFL learners and semi-structured interviews with 12 participants. The findings highlight that learners' positive perceptions of ChatGPT influence their willingness to use the tool for practicing English speaking.",
