      "snippet": {
        "text": "english as a Foreign language (eFl) writing presents unique challenges, particularly in maintaining linguistic accuracy while preserving students' authentic voices. eFl students must navigate new linguistic landscapes while retaining their cultural imprints in their writing (mageira et al., 2022;nazari et al., 2021;Vall & araya, 2023). learning to write in a new language involves mastering grammar, vocabulary, and syntax while understanding and integrating cultural contexts. this dual task can be daunting as students strive to express complex ideas clearly and accurately in a non-native language while conveying their unique perspectives and cultural identities (Besral et al., 2021;Kim, 2020). Pedagogical approaches in eFl settings emphasize fostering students' unique perspectives, cultural nuances, and individual styles. teachers encourage students to draw on their personal experiences and cultural backgrounds as sources of inspiration and authenticity in their writing. this approach enriches the content of their compositions and helps students develop a sense of ownership and pride in their work (lavrenteva & Orland-Barak, 2022;samarji, 2020). as such, meaningful and relevant writing tasks promote engagement and motivation, which are critical for effective language learning. in the ai era, educators face the challenge of integrating ai tools into the eFl curriculum in a way that supports linguistic development without undermining authenticity. this requires a careful and balanced approach. teachers need to guide students on how to use ai tools effectively, emphasizing that these tools are aids rather than replacements for their own creative and critical thinking (celik, 2023;Owan et al., 2023). instruction should focus on helping students understand ai feedback and use it to enhance, rather than overshadow, their unique voices. additionally, educators should encourage students to critically assess ai suggestions and make informed decisions about which changes to incorporate. Furthermore, ongoing research and development are needed to improve ai tools to better support the preservation of authenticity in eFl writing. Future advancements in ai could include more sophisticated algorithms that consider the cultural and individual contexts of the writer, producing feedback and suggestions that enhance rather than dilute the writer's unique voice.",
