        }
      },
      "snippet": {
        "text": "Furthermore, the work of Liu et al. (2024) provides valuable insights into how students' motivational dynamics, including their ideal and ought-to L2 selves, influence their engagement with AI tools in informal digital learning environments. Liu et al.'s (2024) findings underscore the importance of both intrinsic motivation and positive emotional experiences in encouraging students to participate in AI-mediated learning, which in turn can significantly impact their writing skills. The potential for these interactive AI interfaces to act as catalysts in the transformation of students' cognitive approaches to writing, thereby enriching the educational experience in a way that traditional methodologies may not, calls for an in-depth, evidence-based exploration. \n\nThe gap highlighted is especially pertinent for the Indonesian academic setting, which presents a distinct educational landscape yet to be thoroughly explored in the context of AI-assisted writing. Despite some scholarly efforts to evaluate the effectiveness of ChatGPT in enhancing student writing skills (e.g. Hakiki et al., 2023;Limna et al., 2023;Marzuki et al., 2023), the lack of focus on the students' firsthand experiences and their strategic adaptations when engaging with such technologies is a considerable void. The referenced studies, while valuable, do not delve into the metacognitive processes students undergo while employing ChatGPT as a writing aid. Therefore, the primary goal of this study is to delve into the experiences of postgraduate EFL students using ChatGPT and to uncover the strategic approaches they implement throughout their writing process. Accordingly, our research seeks to address two central questions: \n\na. What are the perceptions of postgraduate EFL students about their use of ChatGPT to assist in the essay-writing process? b. What strategies do postgraduate EFL students use when engaging with ChatGPT to facilitate their essay-writing process? \n\nBy answering these research questions, we aim to illuminate the role of ChatGPT in the EFL students' writing journey. Understanding their perceptions will allow us to gauge the effectiveness of ChatGPT as an educational tool from the users' perspective, which is critical in assessing its practical value.",
