          "status": "GOLD",
          "disclaimer": "Notice: This snippet is extracted from the open access paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.30738/union.v11i2.14898?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.30738/union.v11i2.14898, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."
        }
      },
      "snippet": {
        "text": "The potential advantages and ethical implications of conversational AI models such as ChatGPT are explored by Mattas (2023). \n\nPrevious studies have focused on the potential, performance, and implications of ChatGPT, comparing it to other models like Galactica and KGQAN (Omar et al., 2023), assessing its efficacy in various natural language processing tasks (Bang et al., 2023), and discussing its ethical implications (Mattas, 2023). However, these studies have not explored the potential of ChatGPT in specific practical applications such as assisting in essay writing, particularly on subjects like \"The Future of Mathematics Teaching\". This gap in research, thus, necessitates an examination of how ChatGPT can contribute to this specific context. \n\nThe amazing skills of ChatGPT, on the other hand, have prompted people to wonder whether we have reached a point in the development of technology where an AI-driven chatbot is capable of writing or helping write an essay on \"The Future in Mathematics Teaching.\" Chat transcripts that have been altered using ChatGPT Version May 24 are presented in this editorial, which was written on May 27, 2023. This study aims to fill the identified gap by investigating the role of ChatGPT in assisting with essay writing, specifically focusing on the topic \"The Future of Mathematics Teaching\". We will evaluate the performance of ChatGPT in this context, uncover any potential limitations, and provide recommendations for its effective utilization. Further, we aim to offer insights on the ethical considerations of employing such AI-powered technology in the educational domain, thereby contributing to the ongoing discourse on responsible AI use.",
