        "text": "The use of generative AI (GAI) is becoming increasingly common among students within educational settings [10]. In particular, ChatGPT 2 , a large language model (LLM)-driven chatbot developed by OpenAI, is perceived as a valuable tool from students in higher education, where it plays an effective role in assisting research and writing tasks [11]. However, there are many concerns surrounding students' potential misuse of generative AI especially in the realm of academic integrity [23,19,22]. GAI poses challenges for educators to accurately distinguish between genuine student-produced and AI-generated content, resulting in complicating the assessment process [19]. While some students readily incorporate GAI output into their writing assignments, they often do not recognize this as academic misconduct [7]. To mitigate such concerns and encourage students' ethical use, it is necessary to monitor students' work using generative AI and establish clear guidelines for the proper use of generative AI [4]. \n\nDespite such needs, previous research lacks specific, longitudinal analyses based on the usage pattern of GAI in real-world educational settings [20,8]. Therefore, our study delves into usage patterns of ChatGPT among English as Foreign Language (EFL) learners within a real-world educational environment, exploring the future direction of AI-integrated English writing education. We release ChEDDAR (ChatGPT & EFL learner's Dialogue Dataset As Revising an Essay) which allows for the detection of students' intent in their prompts and the estimation of their satisfaction with GAI responses. \n\nThe main contributions of this work are as follows: \n\n1. We release ChEDDAR (ChatGPT & EFL learner's Dialogue Dataset As Revising an essay), an extensive dialogue dataset that captures long-term (semester) interaction between learners and GAI within the context of real-world EFL writing education. 2. We investigate the capabilities of GAI through an in-depth analysis of students' usage patterns through ChEDDAR.",
